  "content": {
    "text": "LIVE\nUpdated 2 hours ago\nTesla Bounces Back in Europe\nTesla’s European sales more than doubled last month, data from the European Automobile Manufacturers’ Association showed, as consumers in the region embraced EVs.\nElon Musk’s carmaker was helped by the revamped Model Y and aggressive pricing. Last spring, sales plunged because the model refresh limited production capacity and discouraged consumers from buying the old version. Musk’s unpopular interventions in European politics didn’t help, either.\nBut three Chinese automakers grew even faster than Tesla in the month—BYD, Chery and Leapmotor.",
